{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripLowerBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripLowerBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Summable","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Field"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripLowerBound.norm_phiBProd_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripLowerBound.norm_phiBProd_le","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdStripLowerBound.lean#L104-L115","doc":"**G3 (unconditional `phiBProd` strip bound).** In the deep-strip regime (numerator off\nits zero lattice, denominator factors `< 1` in norm), `phiBProd = num/den` obeys the explicit\ntwo-sided-product strip bound with **no carried `δ`** — the denominator lower bound G2\nsupplies it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripLowerBound.norm_tprod_denFactor_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripLowerBound.norm_tprod_denFactor_ge","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdStripLowerBound.lean#L92-L102","doc":"**G2 (denominator lower bound).** In the deep-strip regime where every\n`‖denFactorₖ − 1‖ < 1`, the denominator product is bounded below by\n`exp(∑' log(1 − ‖denFactorₖ − 1‖)) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripLowerBound.norm_tprod_one_add_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripLowerBound.norm_tprod_one_add_ge","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdStripLowerBound.lean#L33-L56","doc":"**General product-norm lower bound.** For a norm-summable complex family `g` with every\n`‖gₖ‖ < 1`, `exp(∑' k, log(1 − ‖gₖ‖)) ≤ ‖∏' k, (1 + gₖ)‖`. Proof: `‖∏‖ = ∏‖·‖`; each\n`‖1 + gₖ‖ ≥ 1 − ‖gₖ‖ > 0`; `log` monotone; `∏‖1+gₖ‖ = exp(∑ log‖1+gₖ‖)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}